def attempt_costs(ledger):
    attempts = []
    for p in sorted((HERE / 'raw/prior_runs').glob('*/ALL_REPLAY.json')):
        j = json.loads(p.read_text())
        attempts.append({'kind': 'preserved_full_attempt' if len(j['records']) >= 93 else 'preserved_subset_attempt', 'locator': str(p), 'executions': len(j['records']), 'wall_seconds': j.get('command_total_wall_seconds', j.get('wall_seconds', j.get('wall_seconds_so_far'))), 'recorded_pass_count': j.get('pass_count'), 'recorded_status': j['status']})
    for name in ['PILOT_REPLAY_ATTEMPT1.json', 'PILOT_REPLAY_ATTEMPT2.json', 'PILOT_REPLAY_ATTEMPT3_PASS.json']:
        p = HERE / 'raw' / name
        if p.exists():
            j = json.loads(p.read_text())
            attempts.append({'kind': 'pilot', 'locator': str(p), 'executions': len(j['records']), 'wall_seconds': j.get('wall_seconds', j.get('wall_seconds_so_far')), 'recorded_pass_count': j.get('pass_count'), 'recorded_status': j['status']})
    attempts.append({'kind': 'current_one_command', 'locator': str(HERE / 'raw/ALL_REPLAY.json'), 'executions': len(ledger['records']), 'wall_seconds': ledger.get('command_total_wall_seconds', ledger.get('wall_seconds', ledger.get('wall_seconds_so_far'))), 'recorded_pass_count': ledger.get('pass_count'), 'recorded_status': ledger['status']})
    return attempts

def main():
    partial = '--partial' in sys.argv
    ledger = json.loads((HERE / 'raw/ALL_REPLAY.json').read_text())
    rows = json.loads((HERE / 'CURATED_DEMOS.json').read_text())
    runs = {r['demo_id']: r for r in ledger['records']}
    expected = len(rows)
    validation = validate(not partial)
    passed = sum((r['status'] == 'PASS' for r in runs.values()))
    failed = sum((r['status'] != 'PASS' for r in runs.values()))
    seconds = ledger.get('command_total_wall_seconds', ledger.get('wall_seconds', ledger.get('wall_seconds_so_far')))
    mismatches = sum((r.get('mismatch_count') or 0 for r in runs.values()))
    resource_failures = [r for r in runs.values() if r.get('failure_kind') == 'RESOURCE_LIMIT']
    outcome = f"""{passed}/{len(runs)} PASS, {mismatches} rapporterade mismatch, {failed} execution/gate error of which {len(resource_failures)} resource stops""" if not partial else f'IN_PROGRESS: {len(runs)}/{expected} runs ready'
    timing = f'{seconds:.3f} s ({seconds / 60:.2f} min)' if not partial else 'Total run time is reported after the last command.'
    delta = json.loads((HERE / 'raw/REVIEW_DELTA.json').read_text())
    front = _release_expand("# Measure the shape and force on the same specimen\n\nSelect a bench trial and freeze its CAD , actual geometry , frame , material batch, sensor calibration, prediction and decision criterion before the held out measurement. These two plans use different test questions; their number should not be summed up as a statistical validation requirement.\n\n| Lab query | Perform and preserve | Number and residual debt |\n|---|---|---|\n| Does production predict form, seating and film? | Register as-built against CAD with separate length -/ surface reference . Measure dry seating, cemented film and force – height – time on the same specimen. Keep signed point distances and regional film values . | Pilot **12 crowns**; **18 – 30 active hours** is an assumption. The plan concerns **12 / 51** blocked edges and covers all listed measurement type requirements for **2**. Specimen, instrument precision and actual time is unknown. [Measuring portfolio](../LANE_X71_MEASUREMENT_PRIORITY/README_DEMO.md). |\n| Predicts a regional elevation change regional force ? | Make and measure the same crown, die and antagonist. Calibrate two regional operating bases at 0 and ± 25 µm : **5 altitude positions** including common zero. Measure two crown regions, four neighboring support, total force and two moment. Freeze the response before a common altitude position. | Plan **10 4 scan cases**; two individually manufactured designs require **20 crowns**. Measure two prehistorians and three repeated closures. ± 0,5 µm is the model's adopted error budget, no proven CAD/CAM precision. [Procedure protocol](../DEMO48_PACKAGE/batch25/demos/X85/LAB_PROTOCOL.md). |\n\nFor a single crown height while maintaining full contact, the model is sufficient with **3 calibration modes and a fourth direction**. Three repetitions and two prehistorians provide **24 power vectors per item**, in addition to sensor calibration. This identifies a targeted response column under declared linearity; it does not prove the linearity of unknown tissue. [Height Protocol](../DEMO48_PACKAGE/batch23/demos/X82/MEASUREMENT_PROTOCOL.md).\n\nFor a static load on a person: measure the same person's loaded bite pose , physical scale and independent calibrated regional Newton range. Record sensor thickness, subthreshold limits and raw checkpoint. **27** source teeth have geometry in the example, **0** has a measured patient power here. A single calibrated target channel can answer a single dental question; the load and torque of the entire arc requires more observations. [Construction contract](../DEMO48_PACKAGE/batch24/demos/X84/NEXT_MEASUREMENT.json).\n\nFor screw, cement method and fatigue: tying moment-angle-axial force, regional opening, dry micro-CT /replicate/cemented film and pre-test defect–load-load arm-break/runout to the same specimen - ID. **3 source facets** is available; they close **0** whole physical edges. [Test contract](../PROOF_LANE_CONSTRAINT_NET_R4/LAB_MEASUREMENT_PLAN.md).\n\n## Run 93 active deliveries with one command\n\n```bash\ncd @DENTAL_IMPLEMENTATIONS@/X86_FRONT12\n./run_demos.sh\n```\n\nExecution uses a new writable package instance and shared, read-only local inputs . Maximum four numeric threads are used; no datasets are retrieved. Linux, bubblewrap, existing Python environments and data drives are required. Installation at an empty workstation is untested. Each demo's documented runcope applies: some generators are recalculated, second frozen caches are verified with controls run.\n\n**__OUTCOME__. Total driving time: __TIMING__.** PASS applies to the existing driving gate. Scientific FAIL and UNKNOWN outcomes remain. [All 93 commands, evidence states and times](ALL_DEMOS.md) · [raw receipts](raw/ALL_REPLAY.json) · [execution scope and preserved failures](PACKAGE_REPLAY.md).\n\n## Try the sub-surgical surgery that the lab can use\n\n| Run operation | Limited result | Proven / calibrated / modeled / unknown |\n|---|---|---|\n| `./run_demos.sh X77` | Run same tooth through registration, fields, virtual preparation, shell, control and export; bind **48 scientific files**. | **Demonstrated digital:** rerun and transport. **Model:** roof shell. **FAIL:** design/full axial form. **Unknown:** same-case-pulp/bone/nerv, force and cement film. [Review ](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH20/REVIEW_LANE_X77_SAME_PATIENT_FLOW.json). |\n| `./run_demos.sh PROOF_LANE_FULL_CROWN_R3` | Try **72 designs** in **6 case cluster**; **0 / 72** can withstand anatomy + function. Local deformation restores premolar band on **3 / 6**, explicit stripe and added cross-breed information on **1 / 6** each. | **Demonstrated digital:** separate anatomy gate and spatial contact control. **Not physical calibration:** contact is prescribed from the same scan. **Unknown :** real preparation , load, patient dissuade generalization. **10 / 72** lacks score and is retained in the denominator. [ Review ](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH25/REVIEW_PROOF_LANE_FULL_CROWN_R3.json). |\n| `./run_demos.sh GENCAD_V6` | Separate **247 / 1 728** roof questions and **2 / 18** full crown slots with spatial contact. | **Developed digital:** unlike the source's registered surfaces; the two sites detect false contact. **Unknown :** physical pressure - and load distribution. The command verifies frozen result and run short controls. [ Review ](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH19/REVIEW_PROOF_LANE_GENCAD_V6.json). |\n| `./run_demos.sh X53` | Confirm entire flat intlio plots in **488 / 576** data ; **84** refrains and **4** source locations are unknown . | **Demonstrated under model assumptions:** the tool's neck, shaft and holder follow the access request. **Unknown :** physical milling , installed tool and log. Frozen cacher and controls are retriggered. [ Review ](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH13/REVIEW_LANE_X53_MILLING_TOOLS.json). |\n| `./run_demos.sh X82` | Calculate **− 21,176 µm → [ 11,015 ; 11,490 ] N** on tooth 16 in a declared fixture. | **Model:** interval from target response and quota closure. **Unknown :** physical patient force. **0/36** external straight lines may be used as axial reactions. [ Review ](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH23/REVIEW_LANE_X82_HEIGHT_TO_FORCE.json), [Cho original tables](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25216126/). |\n| `./run_demos.sh X84` | Read **4,229 mm** minimum virtual axialgap; tooth 36 has **1,197 mm** left after first contact. In the external table are **5 / 6** tooth values above 100 N , span **96 – 177 N**. | **Demonstrated digital:**geometry and measurement interface. **Source measured:** another person's printed forces. **Unknown:** example loaded bite and force. **27 / 48** historical sensor lines fails against 10 %-gate . The patient load chain remains **MISSING**. [Review ](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH24/REVIEW_LANE_X84_PATIENT_BOUND_LOAD.json), [Hattori tables 1 – 2 , s . 837 – 838 ](https://doi.org/10.2186/jjps.38.835). |\n| `./run_demos.sh X85` | Generate regional adjustment with **120/120** contained force interval when adopted ± 0,5 µm . material removal alone provides **0/120** robust goal. The model change is max **13,844 µm**, surface agent **6,922 µm**. | **Model:** Signed new generation and full regional [ 7 ; 9 ] N-band. **Tested digital:** wrong frozen 999 N is folded in corrected copy. **Unknown :** physical saving, power calibration and complete crown's CAM . The same contact number **8** corresponds to **1,3/8,3 %** external relative signal, no Newton calibration. [ Review ](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH25/REVIEW_LANE_X85_OCCLUSAL_ADJUST.json), [Wiechen's table 1 ](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e28130). |\n| `./run_demos.sh X59` | Read replica minus dry micro-CT : central occlusive **+60,82 / +58,17 µm** in two system, ten copper/system. | **Source-measured group agent:** same published cohort. **Not calibrated:** general scannerbias or goal specific cement correction. **121 / 148** transmission cells rejected; **0** corrections validated. [ Review ](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH15/REVIEW_LANE_X59_REPLICA_MICROCT.json), [Cunali table 1 ](https://doi.org/10.1590/0103-6440201601531). |\n| `./run_demos.sh X63` | Read preload **329,9 → 253,7 N** at 25 Ncm ; calculate the next opening despite identical end gap. | **Source-measured group agent:** 25 unit. **Model:** **60 / 60** controls and **76,39 N** difference in the next opening. **Unknown:** actual brewing power. [ Review ](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH16/REVIEW_LANE_X63_IMPLANT.json), [Sagheb Abstract/Figure 5 ](https://doi.org/10.1186/s40729-023-00473-3). |\n| `./run_demos.sh X71` | Select pilot with **12 crowns**, **5** potentially trialable queries and **18 – 30** assumed active hours. | **Model:** planning. **Measured here:** **0** new physical decisions. **Unknown :** sample availability and actual time. [ Review ](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH18/REVIEW_LANE_X71_MEASUREMENT_PRIORITY.json). |\n| `./run_demos.sh PROOF_LANE_CONSTRAINT_NET_R3` | Preserve **51** physical measurement obstacles and **5** second obstacles. | **Demonstrated review scope:** requirement coverage. The exit 1 of the completeness check is expected and should be preserved. **Unknown :** cost-optimal measurement order. [ Review ](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH21/REVIEW_PROOF_LANE_CONSTRAINT_NET_R3.json). |\n| `./run_demos.sh NET_R4` | Bind force difference **76,2 N**, regional method difference **60,82 µm** and system-bound runouts; try **174** error injections. | **Revealed source binding:** **3** facets and **15** numeric intakes. **Calibration / transfer:** **0** new full physical edges are accepted. Earlier measurement obstacles persist. [Review ](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH23/REVIEW_PROOF_LANE_CONSTRAINT_NET_R4.json). |\n| `./run_demos.sh X81` | Read **132 ROI mediar** and separate precision from bias; held out calibration provides **180,318 HU_ref** against requirement **40**. | **Source measurement:** phantom. **FAIL:** calibration. **Modeled:** **139 versus 450** observations for nine thermal contrasts without drift. **Unknown:** physical prediction bound; group SD is not sensor noise. [Review](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH22/REVIEW_LANE_X81_DECIDE_WITHIN_NOISE.json). |\n\nThe power issues retain **PER_SURFACE_REGION / PER_TOOTH** and common error of **PER_ARCH**. Adequate contact and access queries retain **PER_POINT/PER_SURFACE_REGION**. Source group funds apply **POPULATION** with their regional support . Sample count , hours and edge numbers are **PHENOMENOLOGICAL** debts: replace assumed precision and time with the lab's own logs. Edges follow the finest common level; consumers aggregate. Static geometry →response is **SIMULTANEOUS**;manufacturing or procedure→later measurement is **HANDOVER**.\n\nAnalytical covers apply to their declared models. Full physical failure closure, unknown nonlinearity and formal floating point enclosure are missing. An affin height response is conditional; the quota closure for finite height errors does not replace a physical residual limit.\n\nThe strong controls reproduce the height/power responses within the frozen tolerances. No algorithm advantage is claimed. An identical administrative number **93** may contain or lack the executable identity of the height issue: identity error **0**, downstream difference **1**. The number is therefore not sufficient; each line retains identity, scope and exactly reviewed result. [Satisfactory test](raw/SUFFICIENCY.json).\n\n## Maintain the divestiture and knowledge boundaries\n\nBy **8** new version reviews are retained **5** as demo; **3 / 8 ( 37,5%)** rejected: previously unfinished complete crown, unfinished breakthrough delivery and final breakthrough delivery without independent assembly facit, exact summary witness and agreed demo. The last beam scenario **1,019891 N at 627 GPa** is reproduced, but its claim and demo are rejected. A later completed full crown version has its own passed review shash and does not replace the older rejection receipt. [ All version entries](raw/REVIEW_DELTA.json), [unready hunting](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH23/REVIEW_LANE_XBREAK_HUNT_2.json), [rejected hunting](../LANE_XREVIEW_BATCH25/REVIEW_LANE_XBREAK_HUNT_3.json).\n\nThe status picture for **52 chains** remains: **PRESENT 7 · PARTIAL 39 · REFUTED 2 · RESEARCH 3 · MISSING 1**. These numbers are planning dimensions. **0** custom manufactured crowns has been compared to a frozen physical prediction. [Status and new evidence bonds](NORTHSTAR_STATUS_PROPOSAL.md).\n\nLicenses are kept per local release: Liu/Hao Demo1 **CC BY 4.0**, Open-Full-Jaw **CC BY-NC-SA 4.0**, Bits2Bites **CC BY - NC - SA**, RadRepro **CC BY 4.0**, STS **CC BY 4.0**, ToothFairy2 **CC BY - SA**. Bite2Text , Pulpy3D and some Teeth3DS snapshot bonds still have **UNKNOWN** state in concerned deliveries; check the used source. Mandible defects **CC BY 4.0** are used in the reconstruction track. Published table extracts retain the respective terms of the article. This private driving package does not give new distribution permission.\n\n![Execution scope, runtime and laboratory queries](PACKAGE_AND_LAB.png)\n")
    front = front.replace('93', str(expected)).replace('__OUTCOME__', outcome).replace('__TIMING__', timing)
    front = front.replace(f'Run {expected} active deliveries with a command', f'Run {expected - 1} demon and a historical status check with a command')
    front = front.replace("Each demo's documented choir cope applies:", "The status checker replays its older status map and does not change today's line. Each demo's documented choir cope applies:")
